  {
   "id": 242448,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/ebdeee8f7872fd1e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Peter Chen/College of DuPage)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the net primary productivity of different ecosystems.</p>\n<p>Open oceans are poor in nutrients but account for the largest amount of net primary production on Earth. How is this possible?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 759253,
     "content_html": "Open oceans are not poor in nutrients."
    },
    {
     "id": 759254,
     "content_html": "Most of the Earth is covered by open oceans."
    },
    {
     "id": 759252,
     "content_html": "Open oceans include other types of ecosystems, like estuaries and coral reefs."
    },
    {
     "id": 759251,
     "content_html": "Open oceans do not account for most of the net primary production on Earth."
    }
   ],
